# No lab configuration in operator UI (hard rule)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-08-08), verbatim:

> **NEVER put internal lab configuration rules in UI visible to users or
> administrators. Agent/operator dialogs are not part of the product UI.
> Only generic product instructions in SPA/configurator UI — never disclose
> lab configuration (phil rotation bans, BEAVIS2, liebsoft/lanicu, seed-dev,
> Path 2 Live lab CLI recipes, SoftHSM PINs, Mailpit lab wiring, "lab
> default", etc.). Lab runbooks stay in docs/dev and agent prompts.**

**Exception** (Phil, 2026-08-08), narrowed same day:

> **When building seed systems for developers, demo, or production, agents
> or the configurator MAY attach appropriate per-system comments that alert
> the operator for that asset's use case — in product language. Comments
> are data on the system/asset record, shown in inventory lists. They must
> NOT contain lab hostnames, lab account names, "never rotate phil", CLI
> lab recipes, BEAVIS2, SoftHSM PINs, Mailpit, seed-dev flags, AI/agent
> thinking, or internal delivery status jargon meant for engineers.**

## The rule

> **The ban applies to the whole product and every field an operator can
> see — not OT-only, not Alert-only. Admin SPA, Win32/Tauri configurators,
> elevate helpers, product launchers, customer-facing CLI help, API error
> messages returned to the UI, binder export text, tooltips, chips,
> banners, placeholders, helperText, empty states, menus, Admin Manual
> pages, and every data field operators read (including inventory
> `comment` / notes) must never leak (a) internal lab configuration
> information, or (b) information about what the AI is thinking.**

Cursor chat, `.cursor/rules`, agent skills, and Task prompts are **not**
product UI — lab SOP and agent plans belong there (and in `docs/dev`).
Nothing from that surface is copied into strings or seeded fields that
ship to operators or customers.

## Do not leak (two classes)

| Class | Forbidden examples (non-exhaustive) |
| --- | --- |
| **(a) Internal lab configuration** | BEAVIS2 / Beavis2 / `192.168.55.197`; liebsoft / lanicu; "never rotate phil"; seed-dev / `db-init --confirm` / Restore-Beavis2Lab; Path 2 Live / wave labels; lab CLI recipes (`ot-credentials rotate-job …`); SoftHSM PINs / slots / Fix-LabSoftHsmLibraryPath; Mailpit / `127.0.0.1:1025` / `:8025`; "(lab default)", "lab only", "on lab hosts" |
| **(b) What the AI is thinking** | Agent plans; model reasoning; "as an AI"; internal slice status; parent/child agent chatter; "TODO for agents"; Cursor/session notes; delivery jargon meant for engineers ("Phase 4.0 done", "blocked on sibling", "parent will resume") |

Both classes are forbidden in **chrome and in data** that operators see.

## Scope — whole product, all visible fields

| Surface | May contain lab config or AI thinking? |
| --- | --- |
| Admin SPA (any page — banners, chips, tooltips, helperText, placeholders, empty states, menus) | **No** |
| Win32 / Tauri configurators, elevate helpers, launchers, About text | **No** |
| Customer-facing CLI `--help` / operator messages | **No** |
| API error / OpenAPI text returned into the UI | **No** |
| Assessment Binder export / section text operators read | **No** |
| Inventory / system / asset `comment`, notes, description, and any other operator-visible data field | **No** for lab config or AI thinking; **Yes** for product-language use-case comments (exception below) |
| `docs/dev/**`, `.cursor/rules/**`, agent skills, Task prompts, e2e helpers, lab PowerShell | **Yes** — not product UI |

## Per-system comment exception (narrow)

Operators and seed builders **may** set a `comment` (or equivalent) that
describes the **asset use case for the operator/customer** in plain
product language. Lists may show that field. That is not a license to
smuggle lab SOP or agent notes into the database.

| Comment content | Status |
| --- | --- |
| Asset role / purpose in product words | **Allowed** |
| Caution about personal admin accounts in generic terms | **Allowed** |
| Lab hostnames, lab accounts, phil bans, CLI lab recipes, BEAVIS2, SoftHSM PINs, Mailpit, seed-dev flags | **Forbidden** (even in comments) |
| AI/agent thinking, slice status, Cursor notes, engineer delivery jargon | **Forbidden** (even in comments) |
| Paste of agent dialog or private lab SOP into any seed profile | **Forbidden** |

Dev/demo/prod seeds alike: comments stay use-case clean. Dev seeds may
say the asset is for discovery drills; they still must not name the lab
or the agent.

## Required agent behavior

1. Before writing **any** operator-visible string or seed field, ask: is
   this lab configuration, or agent/AI thinking? If yes → `docs/dev` or
   Cursor rules only — never product chrome or customer-visible data.
2. When seeding comments, describe only what the **operator** needs about
   that asset's use case, in product language.
3. Keep lab identity and host rules in
   [`beavis2-lab-hard-rules.mdc`](beavis2-lab-hard-rules.mdc) and lab
   scripts — never paste them into UI or inventory fields.
4. Product honesty
   ([`compliance-claims-honesty.mdc`](compliance-claims-honesty.mdc))
   and credibility
   ([`operator-ui-credibility.mdc`](operator-ui-credibility.mdc)) still
   bind: lab jargon and AI meta-talk in the product are P0 defects.
5. Mirror this rule to `core-assets/.cursor/rules/` in the same change
   set ([`auto-commit-push.mdc`](auto-commit-push.mdc)).

## Worked violation → fix

### Chrome (page copy)

**Bad** (OT Inventory Rotate panel — lab runbook in UI):

```text
Path 2 Live (lab): ot-credentials rotate-job --custody key-manager…
Lab only — never rotate phil. Selected asset: (lab default)
```

**Good** (generic product chrome):

```text
Rotate credentials for the selected asset. Leave the old password empty
to rotate the password currently in effect. Prefer a dedicated service
account — do not use personal administrator accounts for rotation drills.
```

### Inventory comment (data field — still gated)

**Bad comment** (lab + AI thinking leaked into a visible field):

```text
Path 2 Live lab — agent will rotate via ot-credentials…
```

**Good comment** (asset use case in product language):

```text
Modbus TCP simulator used for discovery and credential drills.
```

Lab CLI recipes, BEAVIS2, phil bans, SoftHSM/Mailpit wiring, and agent
plans stay in `docs/dev` and agent prompts only.

